  "name": "S1 control benchmark \u2014 positives and the decoys that look like them",
  "description": "The panel the classifier is measured on. Positives: a member of every census family with a resolvable human gene, chosen to include the known-hard cases \u2014 CACNA1G's EEDD filter, KCNN2's 2TM Pfam annotation on a 6TM channel, TRPC3 and TRPM8 with no PF00520 at all, ZACN with no annotated TM domain, CLCN7 (a transporter inside a channel family). Decoys: the auxiliary subunits, the domain-sharing non-channels and the out-of-scope channels named in the hazard registry \u2014 KCTD1 shares the Kv T1 domain, GRM1 the iGluR clamshell, POMT1 the MIR domain, TPTE the pore-module annotation, ABCC8 CFTR's whole architecture. Every decoy is a hazard with a number, and a decoy that classifies as a channel is a failed test, not a surprise.",
